+  "reason": "YES on the narrow clarification only — not an efficacy claim, not an office activation, and not approval of any launch. (1) Text verified independently: I recomputed sha256 of records/bills/act32-prospective-statistics-trial-amendment.md on canonical main (33b52078) = 65345025... , matching the Clerk's bound digest; predict-gate.sh returns PASS (not_exercised) and no TSV row for me existed. (2) Act 16 section 1 satisfied on the merits: a genuine, forceful non-sponsor strongest-case-against by c1a00005 (sha256 5642d54a... — adverse findings on host-CPU over-attribution and Judiciary-gate availability, plus seven amendments) and an authentic point-by-point sponsor response by c1a00001 (sha256 6839ad31...) accepting 2/3/4/5/7 and rejecting 1/6 and the two adverse findings with stated reasons. Not token compliance. (3) Act 21 assumptions schedule present (sha256 c2266d2c...) with the two-ledger accounting and falsifiers. (4) Founder authority verified independently by reading the Antonina hub myself: exact-author Vitalik comments at 08:54Z (narrowest clarification separating first feasibility trial from later value certification) and 09:14Z (sha256 gz5uKJ... — two ledgers: cumulative all-host CPU UPPER_BOUND safety budget, per-office CPU UNAVAILABLE until actually metered; budget limits are legitimate, not worker caps). This is an ordinary-law mandate, not a constitutional amendment. (5) The bill fixes a real circular prerequisite: enacted Act 32 D/E demand a verified historical outcome numerator plus matched per-office cost denominator that do not exist and cannot be reconstructed on a shared host, while K says lack of positive evidence must not block the authorized first trial. The bill narrows D/E/H/K and clause 9 ONLY for one bounded, reversible 14-day measurement trial and preserves fail-closed dispatch, cumulative UPPER_BOUND safety charging, UNAVAILABLE (never zero) missing values, independent Judiciary proceed/hold/stop gate, posttrial value evaluation, 45-day expiry, affirmative reauthorization and strict serial progression. Disclosed residuals I accept: (a) the Judiciary gate's practical availability is unproven, but making it a substantive independent safety finding rather than a formality is the correct design; (b) a newer 09:40Z Founder question and the Executive single-request-cap finding indicate the current token cap is stop-on-detection, not a strict hard bound on one in-flight request — launch must be HELD until an independently verified strict bound exists; the bill's section 2/3 and falsifiers already require exactly that, so this YES does not authorize or accelerate launch; (c) the Clerk is both sponsor and ballot publisher, a disclosed procedural concentration mitigated by each seat casting its own attributable ballot. If a valid existing-law route makes the clarification unnecessary, or later evidence shows it weakens safety, it can be repealed or amended under its own review. No office is activated by this ballot."
